stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> ACTIVE: llm-server started

    ACTIVE --> CONNECTION_ERROR: fetch() to /ask fails<br/>(refused / timeout / DNS)
    CONNECTION_ERROR --> RETRY_SCHEDULE: llmBus.emit("error", err)

    RETRY_SCHEDULE --> INCREMENT: retryCount++
    INCREMENT --> CHECK_MAX: retryCount > 5 ?

    CHECK_MAX --> ABORT: yes → setFailed()<br/>all queued requests reject
    CHECK_MAX --> APPLY_BACKOFF: still <= 5

    APPLY_BACKOFF --> WAIT_DELAY: setTimeout(delay)
    WAIT_DELAY --> TRY_CONNECT: retry fetch()

    TRY_CONNECT --> ACTIVE: success → retryCount=0
    TRY_CONNECT --> CONNECTION_ERROR: still failing

    note right of APPLY_BACKOFF
      Exponential backoff: 1s 2s 4s 8s 16s
      max 30s, max 5 retries
    end note
    note right of ABORT
      After 5 consecutive failures, all queued<br/>requests are rejected with an error.
      The bot logs the failure and waits for<br/>the next user message to retry.
    end note
    note right of ACTIVE
      The llm-server is managed externally<br/>(PM2). If it dies, PM2 restarts it.<br/>
      The client side only handles<br/>temporary connection errors.
    end note
